messages:
marie: FYI, noticed 99th latency spikes on canary today during long-context batched requests. Only on LRU policy. Repro steps + flame link below.

devon: that's not great. any correctness or just latency?

marie: latency only (tails). throughput steady. spikes correlate with KV eviction churn and lots of reinserts. pprof + traces: https://internal/pprof/1976543210

aj: can you paste the pprof top? also which model / seq len?

marie: model: redwood/llama-compat-70b, seq=8192, concurrent streams ~48. pprof top shows ~55% time in kv::reinsert and memory allocs in slab manager.

katie: hmm reinsert heavy => fragmentation. did we recently change reuse thresholds or reinsert heuristics?

marie: we did bump reuse TTL from 60s -> 120s in the canary config last week.

liam: that could increase reinserts when entries age out during long contexts. FIFO vs LRU differs how often reinserts happen.

aj: quick brain dump: FIFO reinserts preserve temporal ordering, LRU tends to reinsert hot items to head which can cause reordering and evict other in-use slabs under pressure. code snippet of current loop:
```cpp
while (candidate) {
  if (candidate->in_use()) {
    reinsert(candidate);
  } else {
    evict(candidate);
  }
  candidate = next();
}
```

We do that under a non-atomic walk; races can cause double-reinsert and dangling pointers.

devon: double-reinsert + concurrent eviction would explain transient growth in live set -> paging -> latency spikes.

marie: observed memory growth ~200MB over 30s during spike windows, then GC but tail latencies jump.

katie: any failing unit tests for reinsert atomicity? can we add an invariant check in debug builds?

liam: I'll file a minimal repro harness that stress-tests concurrent reinsert+evict. Suggest adding an eviction watermark hysteresis and limit reinserts per eviction pass.

marie: plan: 1) add invariant asserts and repro harness (liam) 2) throttle reinserts per tick (aj) 3) roll patch to canary by EOD and run long-context soak (marie) 4) metric for reinsert rate + reinserts_per_pass (katie)

kv-bot: nightly-tests: eviction-repro-harness failed 3/50 runs on debug builds. (link: https://ci/evict/1976)

aj: ok I'll prototype a capped-reinsert patch and a small atomic counter to avoid double-reinsert. dropping full reinserts if counter > 64 per pass.

marie: thanks. tagging @liam @aj for takeover. Will update thread with canary results. :thumbsup:
